cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  A companion paper is in preparation; this entry will be updated with
  the full citation once published.
title: >-
  Q-OPT: Coupled Crypto-Agility for QKD-PQC-QRNG Networks with
  Constraint-Preserving QAOA
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chongder"
    given-names: "Sumit"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science & Engineering and Department of Physics, Indian Institute of Technology Jodhpur"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-9866-8483"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sumitchongder/Q-OPT"
url: "https://github.com/Sumitchongder/Q-OPT"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a coupled block-one-hot formulation of
  network-wide crypto-mode (QKD / PQC / hybrid) and path assignment under
  shared QKD key budgets, PQC compute and QRNG entropy; a hard-budget
  digital twin for policy evaluation; and a constraint-preserving XY-mixer
  QAOA executed on IBM Quantum hardware with symmetry-verification error
  detection.
keywords:
  - quantum key distribution
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - QAOA
  - QUBO
  - XY mixer
  - crypto-agility
  - quantum optimization
  - network security
  - Qiskit
license: MIT
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-22"
